# HISTORICAL NOTE -- a GC reproduction case that this FS NO LONGER CONTAINS.
# Until P139 (faec5f4, "unify typed numeric arrays onto one array-* surface") this was the only
# default FS staging ndarray.scm and tvec.scm.  Those read numeric VECTOR LITERALS heavily at load,
# and car/cdr ALLOCATE for packed immediates (P70/P76), so a vector being filled is exactly where an
# unrooted aggregate gets swept mid-fill (B43, fixed 2026-08-25 in 474e779 list_to_vector).
# Measured 2026-08-25: the 08-04 cuda package binary segfaulted 10/10 during STARTUP on that old
# filesystem, while the same binary on the x86 FS ran 0/10 -- neither the old binary nor that FS
# reproduced it alone.  The rebuilt package is 0/10.
# WHAT IS TRUE NOW: ndarray.scm and tvec.scm no longer exist (superseded by array.scm, which every
# target stages), and this FS is file-for-file identical to the x86 one -- so it is NOT a canary any
# more, and testing a rooting change here buys nothing over testing on x86.  The reproduction
# survives only in bench_results/backup and the pre-rebuild package.  If you need that stress path
# again, load numeric vector literals explicitly rather than expecting this manifest to do it.
# x86 startup proves very little; this one exercises the failing path on every boot.
# linux_x86_64 — full interactive + dev + test environment.
# Core runtime
# R5RS/R7RS overrides (full set including syntax-rules)
# Optional features
# Dev tools
# P123 Part D vision codec.  Host-safe (no camera needed -- llip-vision-camera? is a guarded
# probe), and the host is where the receiving side gets developed and tested before it runs on
# the Jetson.  Its absence here is what made a client test fail with an unbound llip-vision-write!
# while raw write-bytevector worked: `load` reports a missing file and moves on.
# Demos
# Runtime defaults
# Bench WiFi credentials: untracked, absent by default, silent when absent (see .example).
# Peer CA for the `network` test_id: written by _w3_run_network, absent otherwise (untracked).
# [P69] LLIP auth test key pair for llip-auth-tests.scm: written by w3_ai_scripts/llip_test_keys.sh,
# absent otherwise (untracked, and deliberately so -- see that script's header).
# Test suite
#
# [P251] base/host plus ONE line -- which is why this file was a 58-line copy of a 57-line one.
extends: host
features/llip-vision.scm
